#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "126c85b8-d721-5e7d-a3dc-df997bc0b9ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-4732" :question/problem "Consider ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/ba3f1852b12b6f4a246a855c88c9b867b7e750c6dddf350cab0324629fc047c4.png) and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of $I$ and adding $7$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation $R_2 :=R_2+7R_3$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "f8eb89c4-1cca-5f8c-909c-31e9e0fc8412" :question/math-academy-id "e-4733" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$ to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2-2R_1$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/8d015aca8950073c165d53b14f86f0e65a207438ad901ce82f85f65bb8347519.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "6e47a532-ba7a-5692-961b-eabc743d74e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4734" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/375f1950c460b1f310fa279f6d7f203f88ff641000715dfaec192f47d785aa93.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/6357cc2a2526f38a0f0f7e2e7ef4ee7a1a564adfa70264028ff732f44ba7b763.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f22f4bc9-a3af-5a7a-af11-2a1154c83d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342668} {:answer/id #uuid "73f353ff-9c21-5414-8d6e-0592b64625e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342669} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e1653d-049a-5a99-a575-79bb50ac6684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342670} {:answer/id #uuid "5f24933a-8220-5161-8c61-c8f9db24486c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342671} {:answer/id #uuid "601ef09b-7902-5474-ba11-b036602e1d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e1653d-049a-5a99-a575-79bb50ac6684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342670} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea289ba4-c39d-57ff-877b-6ce1dbb94785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b58aedf-3f0d-5c92-904c-dcfbb7d809b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110458" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of ${I}_{3}$ by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "330729f1-97c7-55fe-9fe1-dd3f70a02ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342675} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd0cbc4-ab83-535d-8afa-62a6ffebc2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342676} {:answer/id #uuid "b24c6681-76dc-5361-9295-766ab13053ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342677} {:answer/id #uuid "3aed1173-3c24-5b21-a069-30851b1cb19c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342678} {:answer/id #uuid "83224c01-3bab-53a3-aee6-e81a7ab4ec41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{9}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b24c6681-76dc-5361-9295-766ab13053ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342677} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa34751e-5197-5d3d-867d-209ed9fe548e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52254038-d05c-55f4-b7ec-6ffa7eb5d604" :question/math-academy-id "q-110464" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the third row of ${I}_{3}$ by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=9{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dac3efa0-1ae2-5bd2-980e-cb46486c6ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342682} {:answer/id #uuid "368b2479-20d8-5246-bc95-a36902878771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342683} {:answer/id #uuid "701e657e-86f0-5ecf-a0b5-8b1362874208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342684} {:answer/id #uuid "78e8adb1-8fa3-5a70-b2ac-b5bd85152a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342685} {:answer/id #uuid "5df98491-dff5-5015-9853-dbc99fd74dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5df98491-dff5-5015-9853-dbc99fd74dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342686} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf8765f-b908-58d5-9f68-436ba12fce27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1dd09a5c-8e88-5fce-84e9-a0e819f9a2c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110473" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{1}:=-2{R}_{1}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-2{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd45dd00-0398-5ff7-8cbf-0f733d30eac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342689} {:answer/id #uuid "d6345991-0351-5ceb-9f16-70ae9dab716c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342690} {:answer/id #uuid "4f384f54-45df-58d0-96a8-d779b4befff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342691} {:answer/id #uuid "11dd4d5e-f196-51a8-b6bb-366dbcd7bd9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342692} {:answer/id #uuid "0f916f63-4965-5fcd-b5f4-8141b3f101fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f384f54-45df-58d0-96a8-d779b4befff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342691} :answer-field/id #uuid "79976de3-9144-5a78-9435-02580daabca4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81e02727-aa2a-5c53-aca2-5643c7656f5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110487" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{3}:=-4{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-4{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9f80ee-7dd4-50d3-b6ea-582e5fe20c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342696} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a87281-ecea-537c-a221-931d5357f342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342697} {:answer/id #uuid "aaac07f3-084b-591b-ad2d-edc58aab5032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342698} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e2df43-0fc1-5c72-b1f6-8fe64fd856ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342699} {:answer/id #uuid "01617865-e9f1-5eb7-9d86-5d4abf648668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaac07f3-084b-591b-ad2d-edc58aab5032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342698} :answer-field/id #uuid "761dc18f-d5bb-514d-ac38-191177af3029" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "07a536f9-8737-5551-8e30-5ec5f295958a" :question/math-academy-id "q-110492" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{3}:=9{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=9{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5adb49ef-8bb5-5ffa-90d7-6ffd7b42de3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342703} {:answer/id #uuid "974c22c3-0356-5655-bd1e-9feee3d6d619" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342704} {:answer/id #uuid "545706cb-5f61-5378-bdab-7c17c92cd12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342705} {:answer/id #uuid "f64f3902-73f9-5252-a5e3-fb379ee12f00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342706} {:answer/id #uuid "e38dbbf3-8051-5b6a-865a-b165bd011f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "545706cb-5f61-5378-bdab-7c17c92cd12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342705} :answer-field/id #uuid "97d58cc1-1b46-565e-844b-deff17ded11b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d31e1efe-db86-5d29-87ec-eb9ae72af647" :question/math-academy-id "q-110494" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76a38c7d-be64-563e-a9a5-88cde12b77e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342709} {:answer/id #uuid "a957fce2-91c8-5423-a305-586d080926a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342710} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8c2010-7c80-5c02-831e-ec98c1233552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342711} {:answer/id #uuid "79040cfb-29fa-5d1b-b75e-f70f1b74304f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342712} {:answer/id #uuid "2b64396a-28d0-527c-ac7c-da223d513fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76a38c7d-be64-563e-a9a5-88cde12b77e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342709} :answer-field/id #uuid "73526f9d-aa38-5056-8ad3-c16bda0f3194" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5850f9b5-76bb-54cc-bfa