 "d069d958-32e1-5738-8d57-ceb01abe88a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64e9bfae-8824-55ac-8d3c-9ad9a8753027" :question/math-academy-id "q-42512" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb49650-bf25-5745-84cb-aa8580a82045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342744} {:answer/id #uuid "af122024-d867-5689-9fad-a5c2ffa48474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342745} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b51bc7-ea2c-557f-8b8d-195feacd1cdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342746} {:answer/id #uuid "88f9d4bd-7b65-5c74-b7d8-7573d33a4ebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342747} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c6ae0d-a380-5f28-91a7-e81555836776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1b51bc7-ea2c-557f-8b8d-195feacd1cdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342746} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9cc3ea6-19a6-59e1-9423-b197f861995c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a4110e2-b47e-5634-b8f7-9d3aea1cc0ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-42534" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee26e4c3-0669-5b15-8fc7-b5c338628599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342751} {:answer/id #uuid "258c86f6-8fff-501f-b1ae-074bc657c9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342752} {:answer/id #uuid "ce00700a-55a8-54e3-92f5-287ddd9cbad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342753} {:answer/id #uuid "1491832a-8bc7-52df-905d-feb5e8762a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342754} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd5c545-5b20-5885-b884-6c6b0be72c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce00700a-55a8-54e3-92f5-287ddd9cbad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342753} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dbcdb65-f30d-5c38-a8de-4fa518101787" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "defa3304-fe74-57d6-89db-cdb756b4b384" :question/math-academy-id "q-42535" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the third rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0341b26-9c91-5b8a-a917-20129155e336" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Row Operation Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb1b2f50-28b1-5573-9621-f2935c11038f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342758} {:answer/id #uuid "53f8860d-7902-5ac1-bc50-ebbda2fd4a42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342759} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2b987a-d35c-5eb3-ab8e-91e3b90ff178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342760} {:answer/id #uuid "87f51757-ba6f-5e4a-8b71-8a3253188b29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342761} {:answer/id #uuid "f947e638-8d7d-5ffc-8299-92c09a37d539" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f947e638-8d7d-5ffc-8299-92c09a37d539" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342762} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c07cf12-f254-5aac-a4ee-1ec10fc6350a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1976cb5-7f64-58e8-89f5-a7e4a9f9c0c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75109" :question/problem "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of ${I}_{3}$ and adding $2$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$"}]}
